      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays didn't just wake up on Canada Day; they roared back with a 9-3 rout of the Mets, <strong>shattering the silence of a 41-46 season</strong> and proving they're still alive in the AL East hunt. Sitting third in the division, 11 games behind the leader, the Jays have finally turned the tide with a W1 streak after a brutal Jun 30 loss. The story right now? Vladimir Guerrero Jr. is showing signs of progress, his bat clicking when the team needs it most. The bullpen, once a liability, held the line last night, letting the offense do the damage. This isn't just a win; it's a statement that the Jays aren't ready to fade. <strong>Next up: a Saturday showdown at Mariners at 9:10 PM ET, where the real test begins.</strong>",
