      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The Toronto Raptors have shattered the offseason quiet with a move that redefines their entire trajectory: <strong>Kawhi Leonard is back in Toronto</strong>, a signing-trade that trades away Brandon Ingram, Gradey Dick, and two first-round picks to resurrect a contender. Finishing last season at 46-36, third in the Atlantic, the team didn't just survive the draft and free agency whirlwind - they seized it, locking in Alijah Martin for two more years while letting Gradey Dick walk to the Clippers. Leonard, reportedly wanting to retire as a Raptor, brings a legacy and a final-chase hunger that instantly shifts the Eastern Conference power balance. The cap picture is tight, but the roster is now loaded with experience and star power. <strong>What to watch next is how quickly the team integrates Leonard and whether this bold gamble can push them into the Finals.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 2, 2026"
      },
